426 - I Shall See the King
 / 
Key: Ab
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 426
Topic: Doctrines - 

Verse 1:
[Eb7]I shall see [Ab]the King where the angels sing, I shall see the King some day,
[Ab]In the better land, on that golden strand, And with Him shall ever stay.
[Ab]In His glory, [Eb7/Bb]I shall see the King, And forever endless praises sing;
[Ab]'Twas on Calvary Jesus died for me; I shall see the King someday.

Refrain:
[Ab]In His glory, [Eb7/Bb]I shall see the King,
[Eb7]And forever endless praises [Ab]sing;
[Ab]'Twas on Calvary Jesus died for me;
[Ab]I shall see the King someday.

Verse 2:
[Eb7]In the [Ab]land of song, in the glory throng,
[Ab]Where there never comes a night,
[Ab]With my [Eb7/Bb]Lord once slain I shall ever reign
[Ab]In the glory land of light.

Verse 3:
[Eb7]I shall [Ab]see the King, all my tributes bring,
[Ab]And shall look upon His face;
[Ab]Then my [Eb7/Bb]song shall be how He ransomed me
[Ab]And has kept me by His grace.
